{"kind":"symbol","hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib"]]},"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"text":"class","kind":"keyword"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"text":"StaticRWLock","kind":"identifier"}],"platforms":["macOS"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"kind":"content","content":[{"text":"Overview","anchor":"overview","level":2,"type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Take a look at the following example:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":null,"code":["  GStaticRWLock rwlock = G_STATIC_RW_LOCK_INIT;","  GPtrArray *array;","","  gpointer","  my_array_get (guint index)","  {","    gpointer retval = NULL;","","    if (!array)","      return NULL;","","    g_static_rw_lock_reader_lock (&rwlock);","    if (index < array->len)","      retval = g_ptr_array_index (array, index);","    g_static_rw_lock_reader_unlock (&rwlock);","","    return retval;","  }","","  void","  my_array_set (guint index, gpointer data)","  {","    g_static_rw_lock_writer_lock (&rwlock);","","    if (!array)","      array = g_ptr_array_new ();","","    if (index >= array->len)","      g_ptr_array_set_size (array, index + 1);","    g_ptr_array_index (array, index) = data;","","    g_static_rw_lock_writer_unlock (&rwlock);","  }"],"type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"This example shows an array which can be accessed by many readers","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"(the ","type":"text"},{"code":"my_array_get()","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" function) simultaneously, whereas the writers"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"(the "},{"code":"my_array_set()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" function) will only be allowed once at a time","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"and only if no readers currently access the array. This is because","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"of the potentially dangerous resizing of the array. Using these"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"functions is fully multi-thread safe now."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Most of the time, writers should have precedence over readers. That"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"means, for this implementation, that as soon as a writer wants to"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"lock the data, no other reader is allowed to lock the data, whereas,"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"of course, the readers that already have locked the data are allowed"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"to finish their operation. As soon as the last reader unlocks the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"data, the writer will lock it.","type":"text"}]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Even though [struct"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/StaticRWLock"},{"type":"text","text":"] is not opaque, it should only be used"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"with the following functions.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"All of the ","type":"text"},{"code":"g_static_rw_lock_*","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" functions can be used even if"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"[func"},{"code":"Thread.init","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"] has not been called. Then they do nothing, apart"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"from "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"g_static_rw_lock_*_trylock"},{"text":", which does nothing but returning true.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A read-write lock has a higher overhead than a mutex. For example, both","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"[method","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"StaticRWLock.reader_lock"},{"type":"text","text":"] and [method"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"StaticRWLock.reader_unlock"},{"type":"text","text":"] have"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"to lock and unlock a [struct"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/StaticMutex","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"], so it takes at least twice the time"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"to lock and unlock a [struct","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/StaticRWLock"},{"text":"] that it does to lock and unlock a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"[struct"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/StaticMutex","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"]. So only data structures that are accessed by multiple"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"readers, and which keep the lock for a considerable time justify a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"[struct","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/StaticRWLock","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"]. The above example most probably would fare better with a"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"[struct"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/StaticMutex","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"]."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/StaticRWLock"},{"text":" type acts as an owner of an underlying ","type":"text"},{"code":"GStaticRWLock","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" instance."},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"It provides the methods that can operate on this data type through ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/StaticRWLockProtocol","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" conformance."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Use "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/StaticRWLock","isActive":true},{"text":" as a strong reference or owner of a ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"GStaticRWLock"},{"text":" instance.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"name":"Note","style":"note","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Use "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/StaticRWLockRef","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" (instead of "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/StaticRWLock","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":") for a lightweight Swift reference to an underlying ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"GStaticRWLock"},{"type":"text","text":" instance."}]}],"type":"aside"}]}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/glib\/staticrwlock"]}],"abstract":[{"text":"The [struct","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/StaticRWLock","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"] struct represents a read-write lock. A read-write"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"lock can be used for protecting data that some portions of code only"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"read from, while others also write. In such situations it is","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"desirable that several readers can read at once, whereas of course","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"only one writer may write at a time."}],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/StaticRWLock"},"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"GLib"}],"roleHeading":"Class","symbolKind":"class","externalID":"s:4GLib12StaticRWLockC","fragments":[{"text":"class","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"StaticRWLock","kind":"identifier"}],"role":"symbol","title":"StaticRWLock","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"St